cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Unique-Continuation-Planar: a Lean 4 formalization of Unique continuation on planar graphs"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "Unique
  continuation on planar graphs" (Bou-Rabee, Cooperman and Ganguly, Discrete
  Analysis 2025:16): a harmonic function on a periodic plane graph with
  periodic conductances that is bounded by one on a set of density at least
  1 - epsilon is constant (Theorem 1.1), the exponential upper bound (Theorem
  1.2) and the zero case (Theorem 1.3) behind it, the exponential lower bound
  of the appendix, and non-planar periodic conductances on Z^2 with a harmonic
  function supported on a diagonal (Theorem 5.1).  Three results the paper
  cites without proof are taken as explicit hypotheses.  The development
  contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - unique continuation
  - discrete harmonic functions
  - planar graphs
license: Apache-2.0
